    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0638" n="610" xml:id="pg610"/>

                <head>331. Letter From the Acting Assistant Secretary of Defense for International
                    Security Affairs (McGuire) to the Under Secretary of State (Hoover)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d331-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Hoover</hi>: Reference is made to your
                    letter of 28 March 1956,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d331-f2"/> in which you requested
                    an analysis of the amount and nature of arms which Israel would require to bring
                    it into a standoff position vis-à-vis the Arab countries. The attached
                    memorandum contains the views of the Joint Chiefs of Staff in which I
                    concur.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">E. Perkins McGuire</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d331-a1.xml" xpointer="d331-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
